      "content": "It's certainly possible that the flickering streetlamp exhibits a pattern that could be due to various factors like electrical interference, a faulty sensor, or even issues with the power supply that feeds the lamp. Electrical interference is often caused by strong electromagnetic signals that disrupt the normal operation of electronic devices. A faulty sensor, if the lamp is part of a smart lighting system involving sensors, could also trigger intermittent behavior.\n\nHowever, given that this problem occurs consistently at the same time each day, it's more likely to be related to either a scheduled event (perhaps caused by another infrastructure like traffic signals or a scheduled power surge) or a fault within the streetlamp's own electrical contacts or connections that manifests between specific times when the system experiences a certain type of stress or fluctuation.\n\nIt would be best to report such specific observations to your local authorities. They would consider this information as part of their troubleshooting process before dispatching a technician to investigate and resolve the issue.",
